──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : ChartContainer-equivalent panel (TSGlassPanel) with title "Monthly Cost Trend" + a Swift Charts
                AreaMark (gradient fill, web `areaGradient(palette[0], 0.3→0.02)`) + LineMark stroke (web
                `stroke={palette[0]}`, width 2, monotone) over `cost` by `month` — every region of MonthlyCostChart.tsx.
• X axis      : `month` (YYYY-MM) rendered as MM/YY via MonthlyCostMonthLabel.short — the verbatim port of the web
                tickFormatter (`v.split('-')`, `${parts[1]}/${parts[0].slice(2)}`; raw pass-through otherwise).
• Y axis      : currency, 0 decimals — web `formatCurrency(v, 0)` (DefaultMonthlyCostFormatting default precision 0).
• Tooltip     : web Recharts <Tooltip> → chartXSelection RuleMark + PointMark + a MM/YY-over-cost callout.
• Annotations : web `<ChartContainer annotations={{ vehicleId, scope, chartId }}>` + `renderAnnotationLines(...)`
                reproduced as vehicle-annotation RuleMarks; the source supplies them (the view never fetches) and
                MonthlyCostProjection.resolvedAnnotations keeps only those landing on a plotted month.
• vehicleId   : carried through the model (web prop) for the annotation scope.
• States      : loading (skeleton chrome) / empty (web `noData` → ContentUnavailableView, never blank) / error
                (QueryError peer + retry) / content, PLUS the orthogonal connection axis live / stale / offline
                (freshness chip + banner + one-shot stale auto-refresh, offline keeps cached) — the P4 leaf contract.
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (MonthlyCostStrings, table "MonthlyCostChart"); zero English literals in
                Swift beyond the web-default fallbacks. Keys extracted from source + verified against
                web/src/i18n/en.json: monthlyCost, monthlyCost.aria, col.month, col.cost, cost, noData.
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted once with surface slug "MonthlyCostChart".
• a11y        : figure accessibilityLabel = web ariaLabel ("Monthly charging cost trend area chart") + a stats
                accessibilityValue; per-vertex MM/YY label + formatted-cost value; VoiceOver labels on every
                interactive element (refresh, retry); Dynamic Type via Font.TS; Reduce-Motion-aware fade-in/shimmer.

